FUNCTION isPalindromeBrute(text):

    IF text IS null:
        RETURN false

    CREATE array filtered WITH size equal to length of text
    SET count TO 0

    FOR each index i FROM 0 TO length of text - 1:
        SET ch TO character at position i in text

        IF ch IS a letter OR ch IS a digit:
            CONVERT ch TO lowercase
            STORE ch INTO filtered[count]
            INCREMENT count

    FOR each index i FROM 0 TO (count / 2) - 1:
        IF filtered[i] IS NOT EQUAL TO filtered[count - 1 - i]:
            RETURN false

    RETURN true


##Problem 4
BRUTE FORCE (Upgraded Version):
Instead of reversing the vowel array in a separate pass, this version
 simply takes vowels from the END of the collected vowel list when
rebuilding the String. This automatically produces the reversed vowel
order without needing an explicit reverse loop.

Why this is an upgrade:
 - Removes the extra reverse loop (slightly more efficient).
 - Still uses two full passes over the String (collect + rebuild).
 - Still uses O(n) extra space for the vowel array.

Example:
 Input:  "hello Ali"
  Collected vowels: [e, o, a, i]
  Rebuild using end → start: i, a, o,e
  Output: "hilla ole"

This is still a brute-force solution, but more compact and avoids
the manual array reversal step.

